1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,589
Our rule is one sentence.

2
00:00:02,539 --> 00:00:05,676
If we didn't fetch it, we didn't say it.

3
00:00:05,676 --> 00:00:13,320
Verbatim is a research agent where every sentence carries a receipt,
and anything it cannot prove gets labelled instead of asserted.

4
00:00:13,939 --> 00:00:18,811
Deep research agents hallucinate three to thirteen percent of their
citations.

5
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:24,737
That is measured across two hundred and twenty thousand citation URLs,
published this April.

6
00:00:24,737 --> 00:00:28,018
The deeper they research, the worse it gets.

7
00:00:28,018 --> 00:00:34,060
So the part of Verbatim that decides whether the agent is right
contains no language model at all.

8
00:00:34,670 --> 00:00:37,901
Here is the whole idea in one command.

9
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:41,808
A claim with a paraphrased quote comes back unsupported.

10
00:00:41,808 --> 00:00:48,280
The same claim with the words the source actually uses comes back
supported, with the byte range where it matched.

11
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:50,963
No model scored either one.

12
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:58,561
On a real run against the live web: sixty-two claims checked,
thirty-one sources read, and eighteen rejected.

13
00:00:58,511 --> 00:01:02,000
Fourteen were paraphrased rather than quoted.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,021
Four contradicted the source outright.

15
00:01:05,021 --> 00:01:08,810
Every surviving sentence has a receipt you can open.

16
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:15,414
State is an append-only event log, and every effect settles under an
idempotency key.

17
00:01:15,364 --> 00:01:20,390
So I can kill the agent mid-run with SIGKILL, restart it, and resume.

18
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:22,564
Nine fetches settled.

19
00:01:22,564 --> 00:01:24,921
Nine distinct keys.

20
00:01:24,921 --> 00:01:27,004
Zero repeated.

21
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:30,747
neatlogs is how we found the failures.

22
00:01:30,697 --> 00:01:36,556
Every run posts one nested trace: a span per agent step, per search,
per fetch.

23
00:01:36,556 --> 00:01:43,105
The verifier's checks are guardrail spans, so a failed verification is
red in the dashboard for free.

24
00:01:43,105 --> 00:01:48,457
That is how we found the eight kilobyte ingest ceiling that was
silently dropping traces.

25
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:53,342
Entire ties every commit to the agent session that produced it.

26
00:01:53,292 --> 00:01:58,930
The agent commits its own artifacts, so the reasoning behind a change
stays with the change.

27
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:04,035
Two checkpoints so far, each with a checkpoint id and a ref anyone can
fetch.

28
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:08,066
And cfo dot a i did the economics.

29
00:02:08,016 --> 00:02:15,594
Eighty-three percent gross margin, because a verified report costs
about two cents to produce and sells inside a subscription.

30
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:21,336
Each customer is worth two hundred and thirty-nine dollars a month and
costs forty to serve.

31
00:02:21,336 --> 00:02:24,826
Break-even is three hundred and one customers.

32
00:02:24,826 --> 00:02:27,860
Unit economics are not the risk.

33
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:29,982
Distribution is.

34
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:34,729
A research agent that cannot prove its answer is not research.

35
00:02:34,679 --> 00:02:37,075
It is confident text.

36
00:02:37,075 --> 00:02:38,820
Verbatim.

37
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:41,958
If we didn't fetch it, we didn't say it.

